%------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% gmat_translunar.script -- frozen-truth generation run for the Phase 8
% trans-lunar cross-tool case (exit criterion 1, D-15). Replicates the
% BALLISTIC COAST of missions/tli.toml in GMAT R2026a. Full replication
% specification: tests/golden/crosstool/README.md; provenance and command
% line: manifest.toml.
%
% Why the coast, not the burn. The gate is "trans-lunar < 1 km at lunar
% arrival": it measures the transfer TRAJECTORY, not the finite TLI burn. The
% burn (t = 0..353 s, prograde_hold) is a simulator-internal maneuver; the
% cross-tool comparison propagates both tools ballistically from the simulator's
% exact post-burn cutoff (MECO) state and compares position where the coast
% enters the Moon's sphere of influence. This isolates the coast dynamics both
% tools model identically and removes the finite-burn replication as a source
% of tool difference. The simulator side of the comparison is the tli truth log
% sampled from t = 353 s (MECO) onward.
%
% Controlled-comparison configuration (documented in the manifest):
%   * Central body Earth, EarthICRF (the mission's Earth-centred GCRF).
%   * Force model: Earth point mass plus the Sun and Luna as point masses (the
%     mission's central_body = "earth" with a point-mass Earth - no gravity
%     table - and third_bodies = ["sun", "moon"]). No SRP, no drag: tli.toml
%     configures none.
%   * DE440 point-mass source: the DE-file set the zero-EOP startup file
%     selects, the same DE440 family as the committed excerpt tli.toml reads.
%   * EOP: run with --startup_file gmat_startup_zeroeop.txt (as the other
%     Earth-regime cases), though at cislunar distances the Earth-orientation
%     convention is immaterial to the < 1 km gate.
%   * Fixed-step integration (ErrorControl = None, 60 s RK89 steps). The coast
%     is 455755 - 353 = 455402 s; 455402 is not a multiple of 60, so the
%     comparison samples both trajectories on the shared 60 s grid from MECO
%     and additionally at the SOI-arrival epoch located by the simulator
%     (the manifest records the arrival epoch and the compared state).
%   * MECO Cartesian state (EarthICRF), the simulator's exact tli t = 353 s
%     truth state, so both tools start from identical numbers. Epoch is the
%     tli MECO epoch 2025-12-28T12:05:53Z (t0 2025-12-28T12:00:00Z + 353 s).
%
% This script contains maintainer-machine absolute paths by design: D-15 runs
% the external tools offline on the maintainer machine only; CI never runs it.
%------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Create Spacecraft sat;
GMAT sat.DateFormat = UTCGregorian;
GMAT sat.Epoch = '28 Dec 2025 12:05:53.000';
GMAT sat.CoordinateSystem = EarthICRF;
GMAT sat.DisplayStateType = Cartesian;
GMAT sat.X = 2924.891584486244;
GMAT sat.Y = -5365.244555941103;
GMAT sat.Z = -2784.572181633873;
GMAT sat.VX = 10.21613418693073;
GMAT sat.VY = 2.908044156868872;
GMAT sat.VZ = 1.897305905409768;
GMAT sat.DryMass = 1000;

Create ForceModel fm;
GMAT fm.CentralBody = Earth;
GMAT fm.PointMasses = {Earth, Sun, Luna};
GMAT fm.Drag = None;
GMAT fm.SRP = Off;
GMAT fm.RelativisticCorrection = Off;
GMAT fm.ErrorControl = None;

Create Propagator prop;
GMAT prop.FM = fm;
GMAT prop.Type = RungeKutta89;
GMAT prop.InitialStepSize = 60;
GMAT prop.MinStep = 0.001;
GMAT prop.MaxStep = 60;
GMAT prop.MaxStepAttempts = 50;

Create ReportFile rpt;
GMAT rpt.Filename = 'C:/Users/hoyer/WorkSpace/tools/crosstool-runs/gmat_translunar_report.txt';
GMAT rpt.Precision = 16;
GMAT rpt.WriteHeaders = true;
GMAT rpt.LeftJustify = On;
GMAT rpt.FixedWidth = true;
GMAT rpt.WriteReport = true;
GMAT rpt.Add = {sat.ElapsedSecs, sat.UTCModJulian, sat.EarthICRF.X, sat.EarthICRF.Y, sat.EarthICRF.Z, sat.EarthICRF.VX, sat.EarthICRF.VY, sat.EarthICRF.VZ};

BeginMissionSequence;

% Coast from MECO through lunar arrival. The stop time is the simulator's
% SOI-transition elapsed-from-MECO span (455402 s); the manifest records the
% arrival-epoch state used for the < 1 km comparison.
Propagate prop(sat) {sat.ElapsedSecs = 455402.0};
